Chapter: SpikeMain
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Safari chapter Sky
  cites Poc chapter Spike
  cites Poc chapter SpikePrint

 SPIKE ONLY. THROWAWAY. Prints the speed profile and two still frames' draw
 commands as text, for harness/spike_svg.py to turn into a picture and for
 harness/metal.py --entry to compare against bare metal.

 TWO VIEWPOINTS PER ENTRY, AND THE GUEST IS WHY. The prelude never reclaims (C6)
 and neither arm has an arena rewind -- a native binary has no shim (C8) and the
 kernel image has no shim either -- so one run holds every frame it prints. A
 native process gets a 4 GiB reserve and fits six; the QEMU guest gets
 CODEX_MEM_MB, which is 3072 at this venue, and fits five before printing
 OUT OF MEMORY with HEAP at 2.94 GB. Six viewpoints in one entry is therefore an
 entry the third arm cannot run, and the third arm compares VALUES rather than a
 verdict, so it is the arm worth fitting.

 The eight viewpoints are four entries of two, each named for what it looks at:
 this one, `SpikePondMain`, `SpikeCatMain` and `SpikeTruckMain`. Each is a chapter
 rather than a cite of this one, because a bundle is ONE FLAT NAMESPACE and two
 `opening`s collide -- B5, found by trying it. The printing they share is
 `Poc chapter SpikePrint`, cited rather than repeated, so the four binaries emit
 one format and spike_svg.py reads them concatenated without knowing there were
 four. harness/spike.sh builds and runs all of them.

 The profile rides here rather than in an entry of its own: it is one line, and
 measured alongside five frames it is nowhere near the ceiling.

 We say:

Section: Entry

 One block per viewpoint.

  prof-pt : ProfilePt -> Text
  prof-pt (p) =
    show (real-to-int p.dist) & " " & show (real-to-int (p.v * 1000.0)) & " " & show (real-to-int (p.tilt * 1000.0)) & " " & show p.seg

  prof-all : List ProfilePt, Integer -> Text
  prof-all (ps) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ps then ""
    else prof-pt (list-at ps i) & " ; " & prof-all ps (i + 1)

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("PROFILE " & show (list-length speed-profile))
    print-line-uni (prof-all speed-profile 0)
    print-line-uni (scene-line "pig-herd" u-pig-herd)
    print-line-uni (all-cmds (spike-frame-at u-pig-herd) 0)
    print-line-uni (scene-line "mid-tower" u-mid-tower)
    print-line-uni (all-cmds (spike-frame-at u-mid-tower) 0)
  end
